   Set the secret token as an environment variable in Vercel project settings.
 
+- **Usage:**
+  Your frontend must include this header in any request to protected backend routes. The backend checks for the presence and value of this header before processing the request.
+
+- **Why:**
+  Prevents unauthorized or external requests from reaching sensitive endpoints, even if the API surface is public.
+
+Example:
+
+Frontend request:
+```js
+fetch('/api/my-endpoint', {
+  headers: {
+    'X-Bypass-Token': process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BYPASS_TOKEN
+  }
+})
+```
+
+Backend check (Node/Express/Python/etc.):
+```js
+if (req.headers['x-bypass-token'] !== process.env.BYPASS_TOKEN) {
+  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
+}
+```
+
+Ensure your secret is never exposed in the public repo or frontend code. Only share the value through project/env settings.
+
